From a0112dc87afdcac687a06d983b91e889f8fddc67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martino Dell'Ambrogio <tillo@tillo.ch>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 17:19:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt7988a: reserve memory for
 ramoops/pstore

Reserve 1 MiB of DRAM just below the ARM Trusted Firmware carve-out for
ramoops/pstore so that kernel oops/panic logs survive a reboot.

The region is split into 128 KiB kmsg records plus console, ftrace and
pmsg zones, with 16 bytes/block of Reed-Solomon ECC. Without ECC, a
panic-time partial write regularly leaves the dump unreadable
(alternating-character dropout observed on BPI-R4).

The layout matches the CMD_PSTORE configuration of the BPI-R4 U-Boot
(uboot-mediatek 450-add-bpi-r4.patch), whose `pstore check` boot
integration reads the same region.

A board-level equivalent of this change is pending review upstream:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260528123645.2650085-1-tillo@tillo.ch/

Signed-off-by: Martino Dell'Ambrogio <tillo@tillo.ch>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a.dtsi
@@ -139,6 +139,18 @@
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
 
+		/* 1 MiB reserved for ramoops/pstore */
+		ramoops@42f00000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0 0x42f00000 0 0x100000>;
+			no-map;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			console-size = <0x40000>;
+			ftrace-size = <0x10000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x10000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+		};
+
 		/* 320 KiB reserved for ARM Trusted Firmware (BL31 and BL32) */
 		secmon@43000000 {
 			reg = <0 0x43000000 0 0x50000>;
